	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: The paper describes preprocessing: low-frequency categories were grouped, nominal variables were one-hot encoded, numerical variables were normalized, and the dataset was “bootstrap resampled 10 times and stratified by the outcome.” This stratified bootstrap handling is best categorized as Other for class imbalance rather than a standard reweighting method. Missing-data handling was not clearly reported. The paper states that “the complete analysis code is available” on GitHub, so code availability is affirmative under the available labels. No fixed train/test split sizes were reported.  ￼

